---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Malaysia eVisa and eNTRI from Pakistan — Complete Guide',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
};

const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Difference between Malaysia eVisa and eNTRI?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'eVisa is a full single-entry visa valid 3 months with 30-day stay. eNTRI (electronic Travel Registration & Information) is cheaper and faster but only valid 15 days per entry.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long is Malaysia eVisa valid?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Malaysia eVisa is valid for 3 months from issue date for a single entry, allowing stay of up to 30 days.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can Pakistanis extend Malaysia visa?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes. Both eVisa and eNTRI can be extended once at a Malaysian Immigration office before expiry — eVisa by 30 days, eNTRI not extendable.' } },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Malaysia eVisa and eNTRI from Pakistan — Complete 2026 Guide"
  description="Pakistani guide to Malaysia eVisa (30 days) and eNTRI (15 days). Online application, fees, documents, Kuala Lumpur travel tips."
  schema={[article, faq]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</a> ›
      <span>Malaysia eVisa</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Malaysia eVisa and eNTRI from Pakistan — Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: October 2026 · 8 minute read</p>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="lead text-lg">
        Malaysia is one of the easier Asian destinations for Pakistani travelers thanks to online visa facilities. This guide covers both the eVisa (full visa) and eNTRI (travel registration), with step-by-step application details.
      </p>

      <h2>Two Options for Pakistanis</h2>
      <h3>Malaysia eVisa</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Validity:</strong> 3 months from issue date</li>
        <li><strong>Stay allowed:</strong> up to 30 days per entry</li>
        <li><strong>Entries:</strong> single entry</li>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> approximately $50 USD (visa fee + service charge)</li>
        <li><strong>Processing:</strong> 2–3 working days</li>
        <li><strong>Extendable:</strong> yes, by 30 days once in Malaysia</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Malaysia eNTRI</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Validity:</strong> 3 months from issue date</li>
        <li><strong>Stay allowed:</strong> up to 15 days per entry</li>
        <li><strong>Entries:</strong> single entry</li>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> approximately $20 USD</li>
        <li><strong>Processing:</strong> within 24 hours</li>
        <li><strong>Extendable:</strong> no</li>
        <li><strong>Must enter via designated airports</strong> (KUL, Penang, Johor Bahru etc.)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Which One Should You Choose?</h2>
      <p>
        Choose <strong>eVisa</strong> if:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>You plan to stay more than 15 days</li>
        <li>You want flexibility to extend</li>
        <li>You're traveling for business</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Choose <strong>eNTRI</strong> if:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Short holiday — up to 15 days</li>
        <li>You want faster, cheaper processing</li>
        <li>You're entering via a major airport</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to Apply for eVisa</h2>
      <h3>Step 1 — Visit Official Portal</h3>
      <p>
        Apply at <code>malaysiavisa.imi.gov.my</code>. Beware of imitation sites that charge extra fees.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 2 — Create Account</h3>
      <p>
        Register with your email. Verify via confirmation email.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 3 — Fill the Application</h3>
      <p>
        Enter passport details, travel dates, purpose, Malaysia address, flight bookings, and contact information.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 4 — Upload Documents</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Passport data page (scan)</li>
        <li>Recent photograph (passport size, white background)</li>
        <li>Confirmed return flight ticket</li>
        <li>Hotel booking or address of stay</li>
        <li>Bank statement showing adequate funds</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Step 5 — Pay the Fee</h3>
      <p>
        Credit/debit card payment through the portal.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 6 — Receive eVisa</h3>
      <p>
        Within 2–3 working days, your eVisa arrives by email as a PDF. Print and carry on arrival.
      </p>

      <h2>How to Apply for eNTRI</h2>
      <p>
        Same portal, select eNTRI instead of eVisa during application. Document requirements are similar. Processing is faster (usually within 24 hours).
      </p>

      <h2>Required Documents (Both)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Passport valid 6+ months with 2 blank pages</li>
        <li>Return flight ticket (confirmed)</li>
        <li>Hotel booking or inviting party's address</li>
        <li>Bank statement — last 3 months</li>
        <li>Employment letter or business proof</li>
        <li>Photo (passport style, white background)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>On Arrival in Malaysia</h2>
      <p>
        Immigration officer scans your eVisa or eNTRI. Keep ready:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Printed eVisa/eNTRI</li>
        <li>Passport</li>
        <li>Return ticket</li>
        <li>Hotel booking</li>
        <li>Proof of sufficient funds ($50/day minimum recommended)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Officer stamps your passport with entry date and stay duration.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Rejection Reasons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Insufficient funds in bank statement</li>
        <li>Weak employment or business documentation</li>
        <li>Previous overstays in Malaysia or other countries</li>
        <li>Vague travel purpose</li>
        <li>Blurred document scans</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Visa-Free Alternatives Through Malaysia</h2>
      <h3>Transit Without Visa (TWOV)</h3>
      <p>
        If connecting through Kuala Lumpur (KLIA/KLIA2) with less than 24 hours before onward flight and staying in transit area, no visa is required.
      </p>

      <h3>Visa On Arrival (VoA)</h3>
      <p>
        Available for Pakistani passport holders coming <strong>from Singapore, Thailand, Indonesia, or Brunei</strong> as a tourist, but requires meeting specific criteria. Not reliable as a primary plan.
      </p>

      <h2>Working or Studying in Malaysia</h2>
      <p>
        eVisa and eNTRI are strictly for tourism. For work, you need an employer-sponsored Employment Pass (minimum salary RM 5,000). For study, a Student Pass is required.
      </p>

      <h2>Popular Destinations for Pakistani Travelers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kuala Lumpur:</strong> Petronas Towers, KL Tower, Bukit Bintang, Batu Caves</li>
        <li><strong>Penang (George Town):</strong> UNESCO heritage, street food, beaches</li>
        <li><strong>Langkawi:</strong> island paradise, duty-free shopping</li>
        <li><strong>Malacca:</strong> colonial history, Jonker Street</li>
        <li><strong>Cameron Highlands:</strong> tea plantations, cool weather</li>
        <li><strong>Johor Bahru:</strong> gateway to Singapore, Legoland</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Flights from Pakistan</h2>
      <p>
        Direct and connecting options:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Malaysia Airlines — direct KHI-KUL</li>
        <li>AirAsia X — direct, budget option</li>
        <li>Emirates, Qatar, Etihad — via Gulf hubs</li>
        <li>Thai Airways, Singapore Airlines — via Bangkok/Singapore</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related Resources</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/guides/thailand-dtv-visa-pakistan/">Thailand DTV Guide</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">Fee Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/pkr-currency-converter/">PKR to MYR Converter</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
